  "introTagline": "The Treasure House of Breath",
  "@introTagline": { "description": "Intro screen tagline" },
  "introWhatTitle": "What is Saranidhi?",
  "@introWhatTitle": { "description": "Intro section title" },
  "introWhatBody": "Saranidhi (Tamil: \u0BB8\u0BB0\u0BA8\u0BBF\u0BA4\u0BBF) means 'The Treasure House of Breath'. It is a spiritual life-guidance app rooted in the ancient Tamil sciences of Sara Kalai (breath science) and Panja Pakshi Shastra (five birds system).\n\nBy observing which nostril is dominant and aligning your actions with cosmic rhythms, you can make better decisions, find optimal timing, and deepen your spiritual practice.",
  "@introWhatBody": { "description": "Intro what is section body" },
  "introHowTitle": "How It Works",
  "@introHowTitle": { "description": "Intro how it works section title" },
  "introHowBullet1": "Your birth star (nakshatra) determines your personal Pakshi bird \u2014 it governs your daily energy cycles.",
  "@introHowBullet1": { "description": "Intro how bullet 1" },
  "introHowBullet2": "Each day is divided into 5 Yamas (time segments). Your bird cycles through 5 states: Ruling, Eating, Walking, Sleeping, Dying.",
  "@introHowBullet2": { "description": "Intro how bullet 2" },
  "introHowBullet3": "Track your breath flow (left/right nostril) and align it with the cosmic pattern for optimal living.",
  "@introHowBullet3": { "description": "Intro how bullet 3" },
  "introNeedTitle": "What You'll Need",
  "@introNeedTitle": { "description": "Intro what you need section title" },
  "introNeedBullet1": "Your birth star (nakshatra) or date of birth \u2014 to determine your Pakshi bird.",
  "@introNeedBullet1": { "description": "Intro need bullet 1" },
  "introNeedBullet2": "Your current city \u2014 for accurate sunrise/sunset times (all data stays on your device).",
  "@introNeedBullet2": { "description": "Intro need bullet 2" },
  "introGetStarted": "Get Started",
  "@introGetStarted": { "description": "Get Started button on intro screen" },

  "guideTitle": "User Guide",
  "@guideTitle": { "description": "User Guide screen title" },
  "guideWhatTitle": "What is Saranidhi?",
  "@guideWhatTitle": { "description": "Guide section 1 title" },
  "guideWhatBody": "Saranidhi (\u0BB8\u0BB0\u0BA8\u0BBF\u0BA4\u0BBF) means 'The Treasure House of Breath' in Tamil. The name combines 'Sara' (breath/essence, from Sara Kalai) and 'Nidhi' (treasure/storehouse).\n\nThis app helps you align your daily actions with ancient Vedic breath rhythms and the Panja Pakshi (Five Birds) system \u2014 a time-tested framework for optimal living passed down through Tamil spiritual traditions.",
  "@guideWhatBody": { "description": "Guide section 1 body" },
  "guideScienceTitle": "The Science Behind It",
  "@guideScienceTitle": { "description": "Guide section 2 title" },
  "guideScienceBody": "Saranidhi is based on two ancient sciences:\n\n\u2022 Siva Swarodaya (Sara Kalai) \u2014 The science of breath flow (Saram). Your dominant nostril (Idakalai/Left or Pingalai/Right) cycles throughout the day and influences your energy, decision-making, and well-being. When both flow equally, the sacred Suzhumunai state is active.\n\n\u2022 Panja Pakshi Shastra \u2014 The Five Birds system. Based on your birth nakshatra, you are assigned one of five birds (Vulture, Owl, Crow, Rooster, Peacock) that governs your daily energy cycle through five states (Arasu, Uun, Nadai, Thuyil, Saavu).",
  "@guideScienceBody": { "description": "Guide section 2 body" },
  "guideBirdTitle": "Your Birth Bird",
  "@guideBirdTitle": { "description": "Guide section 3 title" },
  "guideBirdBody": "Your birth star (nakshatra) determines your personal Pakshi bird. Each of the 27 nakshatras maps to one of five birds:\n\n\uD83E\uDD85 Vulture (Hawk) \u2014 Sharp, decisive, powerful\n\uD83E\uDD89 Owl \u2014 Wise, nocturnal, intuitive\n\uD83D\uDC26\u200D\u2B1B Crow \u2014 Adaptable, intelligent, resourceful\n\uD83D\uDC13 Rooster (Cock) \u2014 Disciplined, alert, punctual\n\uD83E\uDD9A Peacock \u2014 Graceful, creative, expressive\n\nYour bird is fixed from birth and determines how your energy cycles through the day.",
  "@guideBirdBody": { "description": "Guide section 3 body" },
  "guideRhythmTitle": "Daily Rhythm",
  "@guideRhythmTitle": { "description": "Guide section 4 title" },
  "guideRhythmBody": "Each day (sunrise to sunset) is divided into 5 equal time segments called Yamas (Yaamam). Your bird cycles through 5 states in each Yama:\n\n\uD83D\uDC51 Arasu (Ruling) \u2014 Peak power! Best time for important decisions and bold action. [Artha window]\n\uD83C\uDF7D\uFE0F Uun (Eating) \u2014 Preparation time. Good for learning and gaining strength. [Kriya window]\n\uD83D\uDEB6 Nadai (Walking) \u2014 Routine work. Avoid critical decisions. [Artha window]\n\uD83D\uDCA4 Thuyil (Sleeping) \u2014 Rest period. Avoid important actions. [Yoga window]\n\uD83D\uDC80 Saavu (Dying) \u2014 Lowest energy. Do not begin anything new. [Yoga window]\n\nThe night (sunset to sunrise) has another 5 Yamas with its own cycle. The app shows both day and night schedules.",
  "@guideRhythmBody": { "description": "Guide section 4 body" },
  "guideHowToTitle": "How to Use the App",
  "@guideHowToTitle": { "description": "Guide section 5 title" },
  "guideHowToBody": "1. Check your Today tab each morning to see your bird's state schedule for the day.\n\n2. Note your Ruling time \u2014 plan important activities during this window.\n\n3. Avoid starting new things during Dying or Rahu Kaal periods.\n\n4. Log your breath flow (which nostril is dominant) to track alignment with cosmic patterns.\n\n5. Use the Breath Timer for conscious breathing practice \u2014 builds awareness and extends hold time.\n\n6. Check the Explore tab for historical data and best times this week.",
  "@guideHowToBody": { "description": "Guide section 5 body" },
  "guideBestTitle": "Best Practices",
  "@guideBestTitle": { "description": "Guide section 6 title" },
  "guideBestBody": "\u2022 Check in at each Yama transition (the app can notify you).\n\u2022 Use your Ruling period for important meetings, decisions, and creative work.\n\u2022 During Sleeping/Dying periods, focus on routine tasks or rest.\n\u2022 Log your breath at least once per Yama to build alignment awareness.\n\u2022 Practice the Quick Sync Pacer if your nostril flow is unaligned.\n\u2022 Review your weekly alignment in the Analytics tab to spot patterns.\n\u2022 Export your data regularly as a backup (Settings \u2192 Export).",
  "@guideBestBody": { "description": "Guide section 6 body" },

  "guidePadaGamanaTitle": "Swara Pada Gamana (Grounding Step)",
  "@guidePadaGamanaTitle": { "description": "Guide section: Grounding foot step rule" },
  "guidePadaGamanaBody": "The Siva Swarodaya teaches that the first physical contact with the earth upon waking determines the energetic trajectory of the day.\n\n\u2022 Upon waking, check which nostril is dominant.\n\u2022 If the Right Nostril (Pingalai/Surya) is active: Touch the right side of your face, then place your RIGHT foot on the ground first.\n\u2022 If the Left Nostril (Idakalai/Chandra) is active: Touch the left side of your face, then place your LEFT foot on the ground first.\n\nThis simple ritual anchors you in somatic awareness the moment you open your eyes \u2014 shifting from reactivity to intentional living. It's a physical grounding technique that combats morning anxiety and encourages mindfulness before reaching for your phone.",
  "@guidePadaGamanaBody": { "description": "Guide Swara Pada Gamana section body" },

  "guideSwaraAharaTitle": "Swara-Ahara (Dietary Alignment)",
  "@guideSwaraAharaTitle": { "description": "Guide section: Dietary chronobiology" },
  "guideSwaraAharaBody": "In Swara science, digestion is governed by Jatharagni (internal digestive fire), closely tied to the Right Nostril (Pingalai/Surya) channel.\n\n\u2022 Eat solid food when the RIGHT nostril is active \u2014 metabolic heat is high, aiding digestion and nutrient absorption.\n\u2022 Drink water and cooling liquids when the LEFT nostril is active \u2014 the body is in receptive, cooling mode.\n\u2022 Eating when the LEFT nostril dominates leads to slow metabolism, sluggishness, and poor absorption.\n\nIf you need to eat but your left nostril is active:\n1. Lie on your LEFT side for 3 minutes, OR\n2. Apply gentle pressure under your LEFT armpit.\n\nThis shifts breath to the right nostril, preparing your stomach for digestion. The app shows your current nostril pattern \u2014 use it before meals!",
  "@guideSwaraAharaBody": { "description": "Guide Swara-Ahara section body" },
  "guideDashboardTitle": "Understanding the Dashboard",
  "@guideDashboardTitle": { "description": "Guide section 7 title" },
  "guideDashboardBody": "\u2022 Bird Card \u2014 Shows your birth bird's current state (Arasu/Uun/Nadai/Thuyil/Saavu) and guidance text.\n\u2022 Rahu Kaal \u2014 The inauspicious window to avoid new beginnings (changes daily).\n\u2022 Day Schedule \u2014 Full 10-Yama view showing bird state at each time slot.\n\u2022 Nostril Pattern \u2014 Expected Pingalai (Solar) or Idakalai (Lunar) dominance per Yama.\n\u2022 Daily Wisdom \u2014 Spiritual insight tailored to your context.\n\u2022 Hold Time \u2014 Your average breath hold duration today.\n\u2022 Streak \u2014 Consecutive days with aligned entries.\n\u2022 7-Day Ribbon \u2014 Visual week overview of your practice.",
  "@guideDashboardBody": { "description": "Guide section 7 body" },
  "guideBenefitsTitle": "Benefits",
  "@guideBenefitsTitle": { "description": "Guide section 8 title" },
  "guideBenefitsBody": "\u2022 Cosmic Timing \u2014 Know the best moment to act, rest, or wait.\n\u2022 Self-Awareness \u2014 Develop sensitivity to your breath and energy patterns.\n\u2022 Better Decisions \u2014 Use Ruling periods for important choices.\n\u2022 Consistency \u2014 Build a daily practice with streaks and visual feedback.\n\u2022 Privacy \u2014 All your data stays on your device. No servers, no tracking.\n\u2022 Ancient Wisdom, Modern App \u2014 Traditional Sara Kalai science in a clean, accessible format.",
  "@guideBenefitsBody": { "description": "Guide section 8 body" },
  "guideFaqTitle": "Frequently Asked Questions",
  "@guideFaqTitle": { "description": "Guide section 9 title" },
  "guideFaqBody": "Q: How accurate are the calculations?\nA: Saranidhi uses the Jean Meeus astronomical algorithm for Moon position and authentic Panja Pakshi lookup tables from Prof. Dr. U.S. Pulippani's research. Accuracy is within \u00B10.5\u00B0.\n\nQ: Does it work offline?\nA: Yes! All calculations run on your device. No internet needed.\n\nQ: Is my data private?\nA: Absolutely. Your data never leaves your device unless you choose to back up to your own iCloud/Google Drive.\n\nQ: What if I don't know my birth star?\nA: Use the 'Calculate from DOB' option during onboarding \u2014 enter your date and time of birth and the app will determine your nakshatra.\n\nQ: What is Rahu Kaal?\nA: A daily inauspicious window (about 90 minutes) based on Vedic astrology. Avoid starting new activities during this time.\n\nQ: Can I use this outside India?\nA: Yes! The app works anywhere. Sunrise/sunset are calculated for your location. Preset cities are Indian, but any latitude/longitude works.\n\nQ: How do I export my data?\nA: Settings \u2192 Data Export/Import \u2192 Export All Data. This creates a JSON file you can save or share.",

